course: dictionary
lesson: 7036
title: Partly: some, but not all
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Partly means not completely. It tells you something is true to some degree, but not all the way. «Some pictures can be seen in two ways, which shows that seeing is partly guessing.» Seeing is not only guessing, but guessing is a part of it.
explain: Partly can also mean one of the reasons. «Many blind people use sounds more skilfully, partly because the brain rewires and attention is trained.» Partly because tells you that is one reason, not the only one. Try swapping in «one of the reasons» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look at the words around partly for clues. On a weather forecast, «partly cloudy» means some clouds and some sun, not all cloud and not all sun. In maths, a partly coloured shape has some parts coloured and some parts not.
fact: Partly means not completely, or to some degree.
fact: «Partly cloudy» means some clouds and some sun.
fact: «Partly because» shows that a thing happened for more than one reason.
fact: A partly full glass is somewhere between empty and full.
fact: «Peat» is made of «partly rotted plants», which people in Ireland and Scotland cut and burned on their fires.
exercise: «Europe has about 44 to 50 countries, depending on whether partly European countries such as Russia, Turkey and Kazakhstan are counted.» What does partly European mean? | *Some of it is in Europe, but not all of it | Completely in Europe, with no doubt | Made of stone and very old | Only found in the sea
exercise: «The short Napoleon story partly came from mixed-up inches and from cartoons.» What does partly show here? | That there was no reason at all | *That mixed-up inches were one of the reasons | That the story was completely true | That mixed-up inches were the only reason
exercise: A glass is half full. Which word fills the gap? A glass that is half full is ___ full. | loudly | *partly | completely | never
test: «Bogs today show the first step: peat, partly rotted plants.» What does partly rotted mean? | Made of metal | Fresh and green | Fully rotted and gone | *Rotted to some degree, but not all the way
test: Sam says «partly cloudy» means it is raining all day. Is he right? | It means it is snowing | Yes, it is raining all day | *No, it means some clouds and some sun | It means the sun shines all day
exam: Which sentence uses partly to show one of several reasons? | *«He stayed home, partly because he was tired.» | «The sky was completely blue.» | «The cake was fully baked.» | «Nobody came at all.»
